#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6e692dca-1bbc-59e7-999f-4acb806ddd38" :question/math-academy-id "e-8369" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =7\\arcsch(1-x),$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsch x) = -\\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|1-x|\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}})\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+1-2x+{x}^{2}}})\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x-1|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd5d1a-eeae-58f5-b7a1-a6a20fb02df9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8370" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =  5\\arsech{2x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsech x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5(-\\frac{1}{(2x)\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/id #uuid "83b6c061-a8fc-5628-a199-60196b904407" :question/math-academy-id "e-8371" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\arcoth{e^x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcoth x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "8a1806e8-d99d-5107-aa63-0bf841cb44c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8372" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $f(x) = \\sin{x} \\cdot \\arcsch{x},$ then $f'(x) = \\cos{x} \\arcsch{x} + g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$  is a product $u(x) \\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x) = \\sin{x}$ and $v(x) = \\arcsch{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x) = -\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a2a32d2-5c5a-5e80-aa79-35a9641b475f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/(x(x^{2} + 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165292} {:answer/id #uuid "b1db3ad2-c888-5c72-b9e4-2ade1defedcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x + 1}{1 - x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165293} {:answer/id #uuid "38fcb69a-b680-5716-8a0e-a99c631036e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/(x(x + 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165294} {:answer/id #uuid "3a785a84-1fec-568b-bdbe-40a6058e39ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1 - x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165295} {:answer/id #uuid "403bd7fb-26a0-5756-b26f-b3cbc715cc1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2)/(x^{2}(x^{2} + 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165296}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bb858b8a-7da0-525a-b444-dc31897715bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165291}] :question/id #uuid "7ac3e918-2f81-569e-8090-bd265690a59a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95341" :question/problem "If $y = arcoth (x^{2} + 1)$, then $\\frac{dy}{dx} =$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc066d2d-b967-54ed-b8f8-371c35e04719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165304} {:answer/id #uuid "023cd180-82b9-5f2f-97cc-1d0b3c92fb24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(2x(1 + x^{2}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165305} {:answer/id #uuid "28d5698f-cc98-5192-ba19-39a588d1de5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(x^{2}(1 - x^{2}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165306} {:answer/id #uuid "48358194-289a-5796-b113-74109d831b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2)/(3x(1 - x^{2}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165307} {:answer/id #uuid "4c62934d-7dba-5030-b6d9-d9c1af75cabf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165308}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c55b12a9-d490-5b9e-a4aa-41e0c6ac6898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165303}] :question/id #uuid "c64b6497-cde2-5c37-b145-e4237792aec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95345" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\frac{arcoth x}{x^{2}}$, then $f^{′}(x) = g(x) - \\frac{2arcoth x}{x^{3}}$. What is $g(x)$?"}]}
